the land may be sold outright. Now, applying, that to all the mineral resources of Canada, has the Government any policy for the nationalization of these- 'mineral resources so that the profits may go to the state?

Subsection (a) provides:
The Expression " British subject " means a person who is a natural-born British subject, or a person to whom a certificate of naturalization has been granted, or a person who has become a subject of His Majesty by reason of any annexation of territory;
A part of that clause is extraordinary, that by reason of the annexation of territory all the inhabitants of that territory become British subjects. Suppose, for example, that the state of Maine decided to become a part of the Dominion, the moment that state was annexed, all its inhabitants under this subsection would appear to become the subjects of His Majesty, and to be naturalized.
